/*!
\page page_strhicfpoint StRHICfPoint

\brief Reconstructed shower position, particle ID, and energy in one RHICf calorimeter tower.

\section rhicfpoint_overview Overview

StRHICfPoint is a single reconstructed shower in the **RHICf very-forward calorimeter**.
It stores the tower index, particle identification code, transverse position (mm),
and reconstructed shower energies for two particle-type hypotheses.

**Detector**: RHICf very-forward calorimeter (η > 6)  
**Stage**: Shower fit → particle ID → position and energy assignment

\section rhicfpoint_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StRHICfPoint
\endcode

Stored in \c StRHICfCollection.

\section rhicfpoint_tower Tower Convention

| \c mTowerIdx | Tower | Cross-section |
|-------------|-------|---------------|
| 0 | Small | 20 × 20 mm² |
| 1 | Large | 25 × 25 mm² |

\section rhicfpoint_members Data Members

| Type | Member | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| \c Int_t | \c mTowerIdx | Tower index (0 = small, 1 = large; −999 if not set) |
| \c Int_t | \c mParticleID | Particle identification code (−999 if not set) |
| \c Float_t[2] | \c mPointPos | Transverse shower position [x, y] (mm) |
| \c Float_t[2] | \c mPointEnergy | Shower energy for each particle hypothesis (GeV) |
| \c Float_t[2] | \c mTowerSumEnergy | Tower energy sums (GeV): [0] total, [1] partial |

\section rhicfpoint_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c getTowerIdx() | Tower index (0 or 1) |
| \c getPID() | Particle ID code |
| \c getPointPos(xy) | Transverse position, xy=0 for x, 1 for y (mm) |
| \c getPointEnergy(order) | Shower energy for hypothesis 0 or 1 (GeV) |
| \c getTowerSumEnergy(order) | Tower energy sum: 0=total, 1=partial (GeV) |
| \c setPointPos(x, y) | Set transverse position |
| \c setPointEnergy(e1, e2) | Set energies for both hypotheses |
| \c setTowerSumEnergy(all, part) | Set energy sums |
| \c clear() | Reset all to defaults |

\section rhicfpoint_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
for (unsigned int ip = 0; ip < rhicfColl->numberOfPoints(); ++ip) {
    StRHICfPoint* pt = rhicfColl->point(ip);
    int   tower  = pt->getTowerIdx();   // 0 = small, 1 = large
    int   pid    = pt->getPID();
    float x      = pt->getPointPos(0); // mm
    float y      = pt->getPointPos(1); // mm
    float energy = pt->getPointEnergy(0); // GeV
}
\endcode

\see StRHICfHit, StRHICfRawHit, StRHICfCollection
*/
